OL,3,GNEWSAHotel no longer housing asylum
OL,4,Aseekers
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Royal Hotel in Hull is no longer
OL,7,Fbeing used to house asylum seekers, the
OL,8,Fcity council has confirmed.
OL,10,FThe hotel on Ferensway was used by the
OL,11,FHome Office to house asylum seekers for
OL,12,Fmore than six years and was attacked
OL,13,Fduring a city centre riot in August
OL,14,F2024.
OL,16,FThe government has pledged to close all
OL,17,Fasylum hotels and, in July, Hull City
OL,18,FCouncil leader Mike Ross said the Home
OL,19,FOffice had informed him the process
OL,20,Fwould be completed by the end of
OL,21,FOctober.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
